    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The term 'Federation' is nowhere used in the text of the Indian Constitution.",
        "Unlike the US federation, residuary powers in India reside with the Parliament (Centre), not the States.",
        "Emergency Provisions (Articles 352, 356, and 360) convert the federal structure into a unitary one without formal constitutional amendment."
      ],
      "id": "36greaf"
